\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3},{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}\\}$ is linearly independent and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}=2{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}+{\\mathbf{v}}_{4},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186360493 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$” is true. Indeed, solving equation ${v}_{1}=2{v}_{2}-{v}_{3}+{v}_{4},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$” is true. Since $\\{{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is linearly independent, we have that\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0.$\n\n- Statement “$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly independent set” is false. Since ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has a non-zero solution, the set $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly dependent by definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$”; “${x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$” only." "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},$ ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{4}$” is true. Indeed, solving equation ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}=2{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}+{\\mathbf{v}}_{4},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$, ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}+{x}_{4}{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=\\mathbf{0}$” is true. Since $\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3},{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}\\}$ is linearly independent, we have that\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}+{x}_{4}{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nhas only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\n- Statement “$\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3},{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly independent set” is false. Since ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}+{x}_{4}{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}=\\mathbf{0}$ has a non-zero solution, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3},{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly dependent by definition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},$ ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{4}$”; “${x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}+{x}_{4}{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=\\mathbf{0}$” only."] [:db/cas 17592186452880 :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1},$ ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}$" "${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},$ ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{4}$"] [:db/cas 17592186452881 :answer-field/key "${x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$" "${x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}+{x}_{4}{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only zero solution ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=\\mathbf{0}$"] [:db/cas 17592186452882 :answer-field/key "$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly independent set" "$\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3},{\\mathbf{v}}_{4}\\}$ is a linearly independent set"] [:db/cas 17592186360494 :ques