endent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+1\\cdot ({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+1\\cdot ({v}_{3}-{v}_{1})=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2}-{v}_{3})+{x}_{3}({v}_{3}-{v}_{1})=0$ has a non-zero solution. This means that ${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “${2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{v}_{1})+{x}_{2}({v}_{2})+{x}_{3}(3{v}_{3}) & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}_{1}){v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+(3{x}_{3}){v}_{3} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ which means that \n\n$$\n{2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent” is false.  If ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0$ has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {v}_{1}+b\\cdot {v}_{2}+0\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${2{v}_{1},{v}_{2},3{v}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” only." "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{3},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}\\}$ is linearly independent” is false. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n1\\cdot ({\\mathbf{v}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{2})+1\\cdot ({\\mathbf{v}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{3})+1\\cdot ({\\mathbf{v}}_{3}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{1})=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}({\\mathbf{v}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{2})+{x}_{2}({\\mathbf{v}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{3})+{x}_{3}({\\mathbf{v}}_{3}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{1})=\\mathbf{0}$ has a non-zero solution. This means that $\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{3},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\n- Statement “$\\{2{\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},3{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” is true. Suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{\\mathbf{v}}_{1})+{x}_{2}({\\mathbf{v}}_{2})+{x}_{3}(3{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}) & =\\mathbf{0},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, in turn, gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}_{1}){\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+(3{x}_{3}){\\mathbf{v}}_{3} & =\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}\\}$ is a linearly independent set, the final equation can be true only if\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe unique solution of the system is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0},$ which means that \n\n$$\n\\{2{\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},3{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}\\}\n$$\n\n is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent” is false.  If ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ has a non-zero solution, $a\\cdot {\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+b\\cdot {\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0},$ then we obtain\n\n$$\na\\cdot {\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+b\\cdot {\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+\\mathbf{0}\\cdot {\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0},\n$$\n\nwhich would mean that $\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$\\{2{\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},3{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” only."] [:db/cas 17592186452886 :answer-field/key "${{v}_{1}-{v}_{2},{v}_{2}-{v}_{3},{v}_{3}-{v}_{1}}$ is linearly independent" "$\\{{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{3},{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}-{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}\\}$ is linearly independent"] [:db/cas 175921