},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =-2\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6-2+0 \\\\ 0+4+0 \\\\ 2-2+15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNotice that we can reorder the equations in this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is true, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$”; “The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” only." "We say that three vector