 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+5\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2+0+15 \\\\ -7-10+20 \\\\ 0+0+5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNotice that we can reorder the equations in this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is true, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” only." "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+5{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+5{\\m