\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false. Since statement ${a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=0.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=-3.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=0.$ only." "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1-3+4 \\\\ 5-6+1 \\\\ 2-12+10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false. Since statement ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ for ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=-3.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ only."] [:db/cas 17592186450832 :answer-field/key "${a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=0.$" "${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186450833 :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$" "${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186450834 :answer-field/key "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent." "The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent."] [:db/cas 17592186275385 :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186275385 :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2-8+6 \\\\ -1+10-9 \\\\ 7+2-9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false. Since statement ${a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=1,\\,{x}_{2}=2$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ only." "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\m