_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-6{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=0.$; “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent” only." "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3} & =-6\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12-8-4 \\\\ -6+4+2 \\\\ -12+7+5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false. Since statement $-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ for ${x}_{1}=6,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=1.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$; “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent” only."] [:db/cas 17592186450838 :answer-field/key "$-6{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=0.$" "$-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186450839 :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$" "${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186450840 :answer-field/key "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent." "The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent."] [:db/cas 17592186275387 :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186275387 :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=0.$ is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2} & =-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$” is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- Statement “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$” is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$”; “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” only." "We say that two vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne \\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is true, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$”; “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent” only."] [:db/cas 17592186450841 :answer-field/key "$-{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=0.$" "$-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186450842 :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$" "${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186450843 :answer-field/key "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent." "The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent."] [:db/cas 17592186275388 :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186275388 :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =4\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$” is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$” is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$ only." "We say that two vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =4\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement 