n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186363384 :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =5\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5-2-3 \\\\ -10+1+9 \\\\ -5-1+6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false. Since statement $5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=5,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$; “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent” only." "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $5{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3} & =5\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5-2-3 \\\\ -10+1+9 \\\\ -5-1+6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false. Since statement $5{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ for ${x}_{1}=5,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $5{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$; “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent” only."] [:db/cas 17592186452518 :answer-field/key "$5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3}=0.$" "$5{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186452519 :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$" "${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{